\subsection{Landscape geometry: why KAN enables beneficial iteration}
\label{sec:landscape}
We quantify energy-landscape structure along four axes: Hessian spectra (maximum eigenvalue $\lambda_{\max}$), basin geometry (energy barrier height and basin radius), gradient properties (magnitude and consistency), and dynamics (PSNR vs.~$K$). \cref{tab:landscape} summarises the key measurements on CIFAR-10 at $\sigma{=}0.15$.

